{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"e161 (test_push_loop_converges_under_contention CI flake) is CLOSED (class=flaky) — merged to main as 0da317b2f with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 (Gerrit change 1167). Root cause was NOT the classifier pattern nor an empty capture (the prior leading hypothesis): reconcile-bridge.yml:314 used 'echo \"$push_stderr\" | grep -qiE ...' under 'set -euo pipefail'. grep -q exits on its early match, and if echo is still writing the capture (large payload, or scheduler preemption on a loaded runner) echo takes SIGPIPE (141); pipefail then makes the pipeline non-zero, so a MATCHED retryable rejection is misclassified non-retryable and the bridge fails red. Confirmed by deterministic repro (2000/2000 misclassification with a 200KB early-match payload) and disproven empty-capture lead (the ELSE message shows the full stderr — the variable is fine, only the pipeline status is poisoned). Fix: here-string 'grep -qiE ... <<<\"$push_stderr\"' (no pipeline -> nothing to SIGPIPE, nothing for pipefail to poison; -iE semantics unchanged). New RED->GREEN test drives the extracted YAML block verbatim with a git shim that pads a real rejection's stderr; the existing small-stderr convergence test is the negative control. Remaining under this hub: e43f is already CLOSED; 983f (network git call sites) is BLOCKED on in-progress bug 01e8."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785600276283287001,"uuid":"52e07d73-bf84-49d0-a4eb-729e2fe03d25"}